I mean BaseMultiModalProcessor._get_hf_mm_inputs: when truncation is supplied inside audio_kwargs, the injected top-level default remains, and Transformers rejects the duplicate.

On this PR, removing only Qwen3ASRMultiModalProcessor._get_hf_mm_inputs makes the following request fail. Tested with Transformers 5.17.0.
```python
import numpy as np
from vllm import LLM, SamplingParams

llm = LLM(
    model="Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-0.6B-hf",
    dtype="bfloat16",
    max_model_len=4096,
    max_num_seqs=1,
    gpu_memory_utilization=0.2,
    enforce_eager=True,
)

llm.generate(
    {
        "prompt": (
            "<|im_start|>system\n<|im_end|>\n"
            "<|im_start|>user\n"
            "<|audio_start|><|audio_pad|><|audio_end|>"
            "<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n"
        ),
        "multi_modal_data": {
            "audio": (np.zeros(32000, dtype=np.float32), 16000)
        },
        "mm_processor_kwargs": {
            "audio_kwargs": {
                "truncation": True,
                "max_length": 16000,
            }
        },
    },
    SamplingParams(temperature=0, max_tokens=1),
)
```
raises ValueError: Keyword argument truncation was passed two times: in a dictionary for audio_kwargs and as a **kwarg.
